        ["A 15-year-old still has dizziness and neck pain five weeks after concussion. What is the MOST appropriate plan?", ["Multidisciplinary vestibular and cervical rehab", "Strict rest until every symptom disappears", "Immediate clearance for full-contact competition", "Reassurance alone with no further assessment"], "Persisting symptoms beyond about four weeks benefit from targeted vestibular, cervical, and exercise care."],
        ["Which test identifies the heart rate at which concussion symptoms increase?", ["Buffalo Concussion Treadmill Test", "Balance Error Scoring System", "Vestibular ocular motor screening", "King-Devick saccade test"], "The Buffalo test is a graded exercise test used to set subsymptom-threshold aerobic training."],
        ["Which observable sign on the field suggests concussion?", ["Blank stare and slow to get up", "Rapid full return to play", "Asking to be substituted for rest", "Cramping in the calf after a sprint"], "Blank or vacant look, lying motionless, and slowness to rise are classic signs."],
        ["Compared with adults, adolescents typically recover from concussion:", ["Somewhat more slowly", "Much faster in all cases", "At exactly the same rate", "Only with complete rest"], "Adolescents often take longer, so conservative, individualized progressions are used."],
        ["Which academic accommodation is MOST appropriate early in return to learn?", ["Rest breaks and reduced workload", "Extra exams during the first week", "Full schedule with no adjustments", "Removing all school for two months"], "Short-term accommodations let students stay in school while symptoms settle."]
